Executed results:

- Node 22.23.2 / ICU 78.2 / tzdb 2026a: all 278 retained transition and guard cases pass against actual patched source and original rc.5 source. Exactly 140 cases receive the independently predicted flag correction. Zero selected instants or actual offsets change. Full Gregorian wall fields, seconds, and milliseconds independently verify the candidate postconditions for every case.
- Native Chrome 152.0.7977.83 with Playwright Core 1.61.1: 37 selected historical/guard cases pass; 15 expected flag corrections; zero instant changes. The browser does not expose its ICU/tzdb versions, and none are inferred.
- Both runtimes preserve the actual Denver four-second fold: `1883-11-18 12:00` has full-wall matches at `18:59:56Z` and `19:00:00Z`; the earlier instant remains selected with `dst-fold` and `lmt`.
- Both runtimes pass six time-known/default/noon/early-year settings controls and seventeen malformed input/settings rejection controls. Explicit unknown time with a supplied clock retains its existing SDK behavior; no new noon inference or setting coercion is introduced.
- Both runtimes pass seven bounded actual public natal-chart → receipt → serialization → parse → replay controls: Manaus four-second gap, Caracas gap with an LMT final offset, Dawson Creek 56-second gap, true Denver fold, Mexico City 1907 LMT, Manaus unknown noon, and Apia skipped-date unknown noon. Candidate receipts retain truthful context, requested houses and explicit unknown-time absence. Baseline numerical body/angle/house/aspect values and replay numerical values are identical. Original rc.5 rejects the three subminute-gap contexts as expected; patched source accepts them. Source-instant spelling is not invented, schemas are unchanged, and engine identity reports rc.6.
- Node observed zero core/resolver/receipt network calls. The disposable native browser observed zero import-time or exercised fetch/XHR/beacon/localStorage/sessionStorage/IndexedDB calls, zero external page requests, and zero page errors. These are finite observed execution facts, not a general side-channel or sandbox certification.

The patch retains strict input guards, Gregorian era/year construction, actual final offsets, the earlier-fold/forward-gap policy, and the three-point sampled-offset algorithm. The independent source copy leaves non-frozen engine source unchanged, and the ownership package diff is empty. No account, publication, signing, spending, production, or user-browser state was changed. Root separately owns full-workspace gates, generated documentation, packing, publication and integration decisions.

The old receipt objects remain immutable records of their original engine/version/flags. A new computation can correctly have different time flags and version metadata. This review does not authorize rewriting stored receipts or removing the site's independently reviewed export admission fallback.

Limitations remain explicit. Exact matching cannot discover an offset absent from all three samples; the retained follow-up includes a labeled model-only counterexample, not a claim of an observed failing IANA transition. The separate site date-endpoint defects—Toronto's 1919 midnight-straddling gap, Apia's empty skipped date, and the helper's year-0000 rollover outside the UI range—are not changed or solved by this SDK patch. Historical records and broad astronomical/date-range accuracy are not certified.

